title: RIP phase-4 proof — a ten-minute soak that is interrupted
description: Six hundred seconds of oha in one-second windows behind a method that never gets there. The proof interrupts the run after the first windows; the load must end at once, the rollback must run, and the windows already measured must be journaled.

tags[2]: proof, performance
kind: performance
target:
  system: checkout-interrupt
  technology: http
  environment: demo

load:
  tool: oha
  script: http://127.0.0.1:44380/
  vus: 2
  duration_s: 600
  profile:
    type: soak
    sample_interval_s: 1

method[1]:
  - name: hold-for-ten-minutes
    activity_type: action
    provider:
      type: process
      path: sh
      arguments[2]: "-c", "true"
      timeout_s: 5.0
    pause_after_s: 600.0

rollbacks[1]:
  - name: mark-the-rollback
    activity_type: action
    provider:
      type: process
      path: sh
      arguments[2]: "-c", "touch \"$PROOF_ROLLBACK_MARK\""
      timeout_s: 5.0
